{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597652331,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65af121001e1iYwN6FKz6Gjz","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65ae53d001f3z1106zNkqKtQ","type":"tool","id":"call_792102567bd8423c97c6d159","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Importing the shipped `.ts` modules with the deep-loop `tsx` and printing matcher + explainer + attached command for a paired control prompt: it separates a vocabulary miss from a wiring bug in one run (iteration 1).\n- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -47,13 +47,14 @@\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Importing the shipped `.ts` modules with the deep-loop `tsx` and printing matcher + explainer + attached command for a paired control prompt: it separates a vocabulary miss from a wiring bug in one run (iteration 1).\n+- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\n \n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n \n [Empty at init]\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Importing the shipped `.ts` modules with the deep-loop `tsx` and printing matcher + explainer + attached command for a paired control prompt: it separates a vocabulary miss from a wiring bug in one run (iteration 1).\\n- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\\\"don't change it yet\\\" vs \\\"don't create it yet\\\"; \\\"show\\\" vs \\\"just show\\\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597646625,"end":1794597652331}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597652341,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65afc28001GGXJ1ZGfb1jodF","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65ae53d001f3z1106zNkqKtQ","type":"tool","id":"call_8beb3d7b3d2b4e78b4f2822b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the doctor hook check (`readWords`, `simpleCommands`, `commandWords`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript`, `runsNodeOnMarker`, `scriptWord`, `runsMarker`) and its test file\n- Why: the dispatch orders this lineage to review the hook check once, after the no-edit gate\n- Rotation status: no-edit correctness complete; hook correctness is the one remaining item in D1\n- Required evidence: a plausible hook command written into a settings file under `mktemp`, the check run with `--root`, its stdout and exit code quoted, the folder removed\n- Recovery note: if the hook check yields nothing new, close D1 clean and spend iteration 3 on traceability and maintainability","oldString":"- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the no-edit gate (`NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, `isNoEditRequest`) and its three call sites, with the final-state reading of commit `846eab66b8`\n- Why: the dispatch orders this lineage to take the no-edit pattern first and deepest\n- Required evidence: a runnable probe that imports the shipped module and prints the matcher result plus the attached command for each prompt","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/r