{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597848034,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65da80d001E0gsww7u1p4y89","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65d8363001XjuNp5Y9AGpze1","type":"tool","id":"call_1a196171eefe4fb68ea65a47","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Run: `fanout-noedit-close-3c-1794596804847-827gze` (lineage `noedit-close-3c`, pass three closing round, area `noedit`)\n- Mode: review; executor: this process (in-process, no nested dispatch)\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Review focus addressed: the dispatch orders this lineage to review the doctor hook check once, after the no-edit gate. This iteration reads the final state of `readWords`, `simpleCommands`, `commandWords`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript`, `runsNodeOnMarker`, `scriptWord` and `runsMarker`, then runs the shipped check as a process against throwaway checkouts built under `mktemp`, one per candidate command. The two settled decisions are honoured: the phrase cost from decision 1 is not revisited, and shell-construct gaps that decision 2 puts out of scope are recorded as edge cases rather than findings.\n- Budget profile: `verify` (11-13 calls), used 11.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:1-357` (whole file; the changed functions are `readWords:119-191`, `simpleCommands:193-206`, `commandWords:256-268`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript:231-237`, `runsNodeOnMarker:270-280`, `scriptWord:284-297`, `runsMarker:301-308`)\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:1-267` (whole file, read not re-run: the fixture cases pin the same launch shapes the probe exercised)\n- Commit `860610d783` diff for `nodeFlagSkipsScript`\n- Executed: `bash .../probes/hook-probe.sh` — each case writes `{hooks:{UserPromptSubmit:[{hooks:[{type:\"command\",command}]}]}}` under a fresh `mktemp -d` folder with a `.claude` directory, runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, quotes stdout and the exit code, then removes the folder. Output is quoted in the finding.\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script, so a wired hook reports `hook-missing`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` -- `NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT` lists the flags whose next word is their own argument: `-r`, `--require`, `--import`, `--loader`, `--experimental-loader`, `-C`, `--conditions`. A node flag outside that list is skipped by one word (`runsNodeOnMarker:277`), so its value becomes the candidate script word and the marker check at `:279` fails. `--env-file` and `--title` are both accepted by node in the separated form — verified by running `node --env-file /dev/null -e '…'` and `node --title hook -e '…'`, both of which print `ran`. A wired hook written as `node --env-file .env <marker>` therefore prints `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` exit 1, while the same flag written attached — `node --env-file=.env <marker>` — prints `ok claude` exit 0. The attached form already works, so the gap is exactly the flag set, not the shell reading.\n   Finding class: class-of-bug\n   Scope proof: the skip is on the reviewed line (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` set, consumed at `:277`) and the probe command is a valid node invocation that runs the hook script named in the settings file; no shell construct is involved.\n   Affected surface hints: `/doctor` hook wiring diagnosis; every runtime row that launches node (claude, codex, cursor, devin); the `doctor-setup`/`doctor-symlink-check` delivery legs that print this verdict.\n   Case: settings command `node --env-file .env .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` → `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json`, exit 1; the attached control `node --env-file=.env <marker>` → `ok claude`, exit 0.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` — partial. The file's contract line \"Exit 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing\" holds for the four runtimes it models, and the four model rows (`.claude`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin`) match the checkout. The finding shows one valid launch shape inside that stated contract is misclassified; no packet acceptance row was read this iteration.\n- `checklist_evidence` — pending (synthesis iteration).\n- `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` — pending.\n- `playbook_capability` — notApplicable: the check is a CLI script with no playbook surface.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:348-355` is the process entry; `main` returns 1 when any row is `hook-missing`, so the misread reaches the operator as a failed diagnostic, not just a log line.\n- The four model rows at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-68` name the settings files this check reads; the claude fixture used `.claude/settings.json` and the `hooks.UserPromptSubmit[].hooks[]` shape that `.claude/settings.json` in this checkout carries.\n- No consumer of the check was edited; the probe wrote only under `mktemp` and removed each folder.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- `bash -o pipefail -c 'node <marker>'` and `command node <marker>` also print `hook-missing`. Both are valid shell forms that run the hook, but they are shell-grammar gaps, and settled decision 2 puts the check's standing as a non-parser out of scope for this review. Recorded here, not reported as findings.\n- `node --max-old-space-size 4096 <marker>` also prints `hook-missing`, but node itself rejects that separated form (`Error: illegal value for flag --max-old-space-size`), so the check's verdict matches the runtime's and the case is not a defect.\n- `--title` is a weaker real-world case than `--env-file`; it is included only to show the gap is the flag set rather than one flag's spelling.\n- The quoted-value case `node --eval\"1\" <marker>` (pass-three `NE3-P2-003`) is still open as a settled sub-case: decision 2 says a command node would reject it, so it is not re-reported.\n- Prior hook finding `DR2-P2-005` (env/node/bash -lc wrappers) is closed: those forms print `ok claude` in the probe and in the suite.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- Quoted scripts, env prefixes, `bash -lc`/`zsh -c` wrappers, brace groups, subshells, `exec`, separators stuck to the previous word, semicolons, background `&`, and the backslash-newline continuation all print `ok claude` in the probe and in `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:56-245`.\n- `node -e`, `node -e1`, `node --eval=1`, `node --print=1` and `node --check` are all rejected as non-launches, so the pass-three attached-value fix holds.\n- `--conditions development` (separated) prints `ok claude` because `--conditions` is in the argument-taking set; this is the control that proves the set, not the reading of the next word, is what decides the verdict.\n- Unreadable or absent settings JSON degrades to `hook-missing` without throwing; the check never writes the inspected file (the suite asserts the file is unchanged at `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:49-53`).\n- A marker that only appears in a description or an echo is not counted, because `collectCommands` reads only `type: \"command\"` entries and `runsNodeOnMarker` requires node to stand at a command start.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A crash or hang.** The probe ran twelve fixtures; `readWords` advances on every branch, the unterminated-quote branch returns early, and `runsMarker` caps recursion at depth 2. `main` catches a thrown error and exits 2.\n- **A stateful matcher or a `lastIndex` bug.** `readWords` builds fresh arrays per call; the check is a one-shot process.\n- **A false positive from `endsWith(marker)`.** The probe's `node ./<marker>` and `node <marker>` forms both end at the marker; no tested non-launch ends with the marker without running it.\n- **The four test loops being vacuous.** Each launch case fails today if the shell reading regresses (e.g. removing `&` as a separator breaks `cd /tmp & node <marker>`), and each `hook-missing` case has a positive control in the suite.\n- **The `--env-file` gap being the settled quoted-value case.** The separated form is a clean word boundary, and node accepts it as written; it is neither an attached value nor an unknown flag.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\n- Focus area: the two changed modules against their pinning tests and the packet's spec/report claims; comment accuracy on the changed lines; and a re-read of `NC3-P1-001` for any contradicting evidence\n- Reason: correctness coverage for both review areas is complete; the remaining dimensions are the synthesis obligations\n- Rotation status: D1 complete for the no-edit gate and the hook check; D3 and D4 not started\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: nothing blocked; the probe-fixture method stays available for a re-check if a finding is disputed\n- Required evidence: the findings registry totals, the iteration verdicts, and the exact spec/report lines the changed code implements\n- Recovery note: the `Review verdict` line stays CONDITIONAL while `NC3-P1-001` is active\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Run: `fanout-noedit-close-3c-1794596804847-827gze` (lineage `noedit-close-3c`, pass three closing round, area `noedit`)\\n- Mode: review; executor: this process (in-process, no nested dispatch)\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Review focus addressed: the dispatch orders this lineage to review the doctor hook check once, after the no-edit gate. This iteration reads the final state of `readWords`, `simpleCommands`, `commandWords`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript`, `runsNodeOnMarker`, `scriptWord` and `runsMarker`, then runs the shipped check as a process against throwaway checkouts built under `mktemp`, one per candidate command. The two settled decisions are honoured: the phrase cost from decision 1 is not revisited, and shell-construct gaps that decision 2 puts out of scope are recorded as edge cases rather than findings.\\n- Budget profile: `verify` (11-13 calls), used 11.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:1-357` (whole file; the changed functions are `readWords:119-191`, `simpleCommands:193-206`, `commandWords:256-268`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript:231-237`, `runsNodeOnMarker:270-280`, `scriptWord:284-297`, `runsMarker:301-308`)\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:1-267` (whole file, read not re-run: the fixture cases pin the same launch shapes the probe exercised)\\n- Commit `860610d783` diff for `nodeFlagSkipsScript`\\n- Executed: `bash .../probes/hook-probe.sh` — each case writes `{hooks:{UserPromptSubmit:[{hooks:[{type:\\\"command\\\",command}]}]}}` under a fresh `mktemp -d` folder with a `.claude` directory, runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root <folder>`, quotes stdout and the exit code, then removes the folder. Output is quoted in the finding.\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script, so a wired hook reports `hook-missing`** -- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` -- `NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT` lists the flags whose next word is their own argument: `-r`, `--require`, `--import`, `--loader`, `--experimental-loader`, `-C`, `--conditions`. A node flag outside that list is skipped by one word (`runsNodeOnMarker:277`), so its value becomes the candidate script word and the marker check at `:279` fails. `--env-file` and `--title` are both accepted by node in the separated form — verified by running `node --env-file /dev/null -e '…'` and `node --title hook -e '…'`, both of which print `ran`. A wired hook written as `node --env-file .env <marker>` therefore prints `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json` exit 1, while the same flag written attached — `node --env-file=.env <marker>` — prints `ok claude` exit 0. The attached form already works, so the gap is exactly the flag set, not the shell reading.\\n   Finding class: class-of-bug\\n   Scope proof: the skip is on the reviewed line (`hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` set, consumed at `:277`) and the probe command is a valid node invocation that runs the hook script named in the settings file; no shell construct is involved.\\n   Affected surface hints: `/doctor` hook wiring diagnosis; every runtime row that launches node (claude, codex, cursor, devin); the `doctor-setup`/`doctor-symlink-check` delivery legs that print this verdict.\\n   Case: settings command `node --env-file .env .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` → `hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json`, exit 1; the attached control `node --env-file=.env <marker>` → `ok claude`, exit 0.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` — partial. The file's contract line \\\"Exit 0 when every installed runtime carries its entry, 1 when one is missing\\\" holds for the four runtimes it models, and the four model rows (`.claude`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin`) match the checkout. The finding shows one valid launch shape inside that stated contract is misclassified; no packet acceptance row was read this iteration.\\n- `checklist_evidence` — pending (synthesis iteration).\\n- `skill_agent`, `agent_cross_runtime`, `feature_catalog_code` — pending.\\n- `playbook_capability` — notApplicable: the check is a CLI script with no playbook surface.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:348-355` is the process entry; `main` returns 1 when any row is `hook-missing`, so the misread reaches the operator as a failed diagnostic, not just a log line.\\n- The four model rows at `hook-wiring-check.cjs:39-68` name the settings files this check reads; the claude fixture used `.claude/settings.json` and the `hooks.UserPromptSubmit[].hooks[]` shape that `.claude/settings.json` in this checkout carries.\\n- No consumer of the check was edited; the probe wrote only under `mktemp` and removed each folder.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- `bash -o pipefail -c 'node <marker>'` and `command node <marker>` also print `hook-missing`. Both are valid shell forms that run the hook, but they are shell-grammar gaps, and settled decision 2 puts the check's standing as a non-parser out of scope for this review. Recorded here, not reported as findings.\\n- `node --max-old-space-size 4096 <marker>` also prints `hook-missing`, but node itself rejects that separated form (`Error: illegal value for flag --max-old-space-size`), so the check's verdict matches the runtime's and the case is not a defect.\\n- `--title` is a weaker real-world case than `--env-file`; it is included only to show the gap is the flag set rather than one flag's spelling.\\n- The quoted-value case `node --eval\\\"1\\\" <marker>` (pass-three `NE3-P2-003`) is still open as a settled sub-case: decision 2 says a command node would reject it, so it is not re-reported.\\n- Prior hook finding `DR2-P2-005` (env/node/bash -lc wrappers) is closed: those forms print `ok claude` in the probe and in the suite.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- Quoted scripts, env prefixes, `bash -lc`/`zsh -c` wrappers, brace groups, subshells, `exec`, separators stuck to the previous word, semicolons, background `&`, and the backslash-newline continuation all print `ok claude` in the probe and in `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:56-245`.\\n- `node -e`, `node -e1`, `node --eval=1`, `node --print=1` and `node --check` are all rejected as non-launches, so the pass-three attached-value fix holds.\\n- `--conditions development` (separated) prints `ok claude` because `--conditions` is in the argument-taking set; this is the control that proves the set, not the reading of the next word, is what decides the verdict.\\n- Unreadable or absent settings JSON degrades to `hook-missing` without throwing; the check never writes the inspected file (the suite asserts the file is unchanged at `hook-wiring-check.test.cjs:49-53`).\\n- A marker that only appears in a description or an echo is not counted, because `collectCommands` reads only `type: \\\"command\\\"` entries and `runsNodeOnMarker` requires node to stand at a command start.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A crash or hang.** The probe ran twelve fixtures; `readWords` advances on every branch, the unterminated-quote branch returns early, and `runsMarker` caps recursion at depth 2. `main` catches a thrown error and exits 2.\\n- **A stateful matcher or a `lastIndex` bug.** `readWords` builds fresh arrays per call; the check is a one-shot process.\\n- **A false positive from `endsWith(marker)`.** The probe's `node ./<marker>` and `node <marker>` forms both end at the marker; no tested non-launch ends with the marker without running it.\\n- **The four test loops being vacuous.** Each launch case fails today if the shell reading regresses (e.g. removing `&` as a separator breaks `cd /tmp & node <marker>`), and each `hook-missing` case has a positive control in the suite.\\n- **The `--env-file` gap being the settled quoted-value case.** The separated form is a clean word boundary, and node accepts it as written; it is neither an attached value nor an unknown flag.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability and maintainability\\n- Focus area: the two changed modules against their pinning tests and the packet's spec/report claims; comment accuracy on the changed lines; and a re-read of `NC3-P1-001` for any contradicting evidence\\n- Reason: correctness coverage for both review areas is complete; the remaining dimensions are the synthesis obligations\\n- Rotation status: D1 complete for the no-edit gate and the hook check; D3 and D4 not started\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: nothing blocked; the probe-fixture method stays available for a re-check if a finding is disputed\\n- Required evidence: the findings registry totals, the iteration verdicts, and the exact spec/report lines the changed code implements\\n- Recovery note: the `Review verdict` line stays CONDITIONAL while `NC3-P1-001` is active\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597824525,"end":1794597848034}}}}
