ions): 1\n39-- Resolved: 0\n40-\n41-<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n42-## 8. WHAT WORKED\n43-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- Code changes of any kind; this lineage writes only its own state files.\n- Holdout prompt text: never opened, never read.\n- The full suite, builds, daemons and model CLIs.\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence at 0.10 weighted new-finding ratio, or three iterations, whichever comes first.\n- A P0 finding stops the loop at synthesis and forces `Review verdict: FAIL`.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 1\n- P2 (Suggestions): 1\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Importing the shipped `.ts` modules with the deep-loop `tsx` and printing matcher + explainer + attached command for a paired control prompt: it separates a vocabulary miss from a wiring bug in one run (iteration 1).\n- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\n....\n35:## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n36-- P0 (Blockers): 0\n37-- P1 (Required): 1\n38-- P2 (Suggestions): 1\n39-- Resolved: 0\n40-\n41-<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n42-## 8. WHAT WORKED\n43-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '20,45p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md; echo ....; grep -n \\\"RUNNING FINDINGS\\\" -A 8 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build