{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597876208,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65e60e5002meTEjCWpOHVkzh","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65e4b9d001ANf6b0knJr3nZE","type":"tool","id":"call_43accefd1bd7488a8c90ba8b","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\n- Building one throwaway checkout per candidate hook command under `mktemp` and running the shipped check as a process: it gives a real stdout and exit code per case, and the attached-vs-separated node-flag pair isolates the flag set from the shell reading (iteration 2).\n- Verifying each candidate flag against the runtime first (`node --env-file /dev/null -e …`, `node --title hook -e …`): it removed `--max-old-space-size` from the finding because node rejects that form, leaving only commands that really run (iteration 2).","oldString":"- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -42,8 +42,10 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Importing the shipped `.ts` modules with the deep-loop `tsx` and printing matcher + explainer + attached command for a paired control prompt: it separates a vocabulary miss from a wiring bug in one run (iteration 1).\n - Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\"don't change it yet\" vs \"don't create it yet\"; \"show\" vs \"just show\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\n+- Building one throwaway checkout per candidate hook command under `mktemp` and running the shipped check as a process: it gives a real stdout and exit code per case, and the attached-vs-separated node-flag pair isolates the flag set from the shell reading (iteration 2).\n+- Verifying each candidate flag against the runtime first (`node --env-file /dev/null -e …`, `node --title hook -e …`): it removed `--max-old-space-size` from the finding because node rejects that form, leaving only commands that really run (iteration 2).\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\\\"don't change it yet\\\" vs \\\"don't create it yet\\\"; \\\"show\\\" vs \\\"just show\\\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\\n- Building one throwaway checkout per candidate hook command under `mktemp` and running the shipped check as a process: it gives a real stdout and exit code per case, and the attached-vs-separated node-flag pair isolates the flag set from the shell reading (iteration 2).\\n- Verifying each candidate flag against the runtime first (`node --env-file /dev/null -e …`, `node --title hook -e …`): it removed `--max-old-space-size` from the finding because node rejects that form, leaving only commands that really run (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"- Pairing every probe with a control that differs by one word (\\\"don't change it yet\\\" vs \\\"don't create it yet\\\"; \\\"show\\\" vs \\\"just show\\\"): it proves the difference is the matcher, not the route (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597871845,"end":1794597876208}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597876211,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65e6a26001eNwN40ZpOMahTl","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65e4b9d001ANf6b0knJr3nZE","type":"tool","id":"call_4abac18b957b4d7480842560","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\n- Treating the first `hook-missing` case as a finding: `bash -o pipefail -c` and `command node` are valid but are shell-grammar gaps that settled decision 2 puts out of scope, and `node --max-old-space-size 4096` is rejected by node itself. Only the separated node-flag case survived as a finding (iteration 2).","oldString":"- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -48,8 +48,9 @@\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n - Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\n+- Treating the first `hook-missing` case as a finding: `bash -o pipefail -c` and `command node` are valid but are shell-grammar gaps that settled decision 2 puts out of scope, and `node --max-old-space-size 4096` is rejected by node itself. Only the separated node-flag case survived as a finding (iteration 2).\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n ### **A `lastIndex` state bug.** `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` has no global flag, and the direct `.test` call at `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:49` is stable. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\\n- Treating the first `hook-missing` case as a finding: `bash -o pipefail -c` and `command node` are valid but are shell-grammar gaps that settled decision 2 puts out of scope, and `node --max-old-space-size 4096` is rejected by node itself. Only the separated node-flag case survived as a finding (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"- Reading the matcher alone without checking `isReadOnlyExplainer`: a no-edit prompt with a read-only verb is held at the explainer floor, so a verb-list miss there has no route to attach to. The probe was changed to a naming prompt with no read-only verb before the finding was trusted (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597874214,"end":1794597876211}}}}
