{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597931395,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65f447b002nyvZIrjisJgTiH","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65f0c2f001gT08TMqAGLSMuo","type":"tool","id":"call_178f376ee5c9400b90ccfca0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && grep -rn \"NO_EDIT\\|no-edit\\|no edit\\|make no changes\\|just show\" $S --include=*.md | grep -v review/ | head -20; echo \"=== hook check docs\"; grep -rn \"hook-wiring-check\" .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.md --include=*.yaml | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:50:A fault in the middle of an embed now ends in a verified restore or a printed reason why not, and it exits 3. The hub attach path no longer offers a writing command on a no-edit prompt, a file name or a mention of another deep-loop command. The renderer tests pass inside a dispatched child. A live behaviour arm now runs only in a marked arena with an allowlisted environment.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:56:`command-attach.ts` now owns `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, and `fusion.ts` imports it. The deep-loop gate opens only for the command being attached or for depth wording. A dot or a slash followed by a word character continues a file name, so `/create:skill.md` is no typed command. The deriver no longer emits `COMMAND_POLICIES`, and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` is the one attach-path table.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:72:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modified, Created | The shared no-edit pattern, the deep-loop gate, the file-name boundary and the absent policy table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:73:| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modified | Imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and drops an empty branch |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:112:| The shared `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` pattern stays as it is. This was decided without the operator, under goal decision D1, with no code change | A prompt that only limits the scope of a change, such as \"create a skill and do not change the existing skills\", keeps its skill and loses the command. That fails toward no offer and matches what the scorer path already did |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:135:| T058 probes | `main returned 3`, `restored line: true`, `after: CLAUDE.md`, `plan exit=2` with `ci.yml` digests `b8ae3686e91b` before and after, `undefined` on the no-edit, `/deep:ai-council` and file-name lines, `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in module -> false`, `(needs a mode)` and `(parent-named only)` on the two render lines and 15 `apply exit 0` lines |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:161:4. **A third copy of the no-edit wording remains.** `scorer/text.ts` line 148 keeps its own pattern. The plan records it, and this phase may not edit that file.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the prompt `use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet`, When the hub attach runs on its single `sk-create-skill` route, Then no command is attached, and `FU` reads the same `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` | `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` and `rg -c \"semantic \\(code\" $FU` print nothing. Met 2026-11-13: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports `14 passed (14)`, and both `rg -c` commands on `FU` print nothing and exit 1. `probe-attach.mts` prints `-> undefined` for the no-edit prompt. | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:88:| AC-033 | REQ-033 | Given `advisor-recommend.md`, When it is read, Then it gives the row shape with `mutating?`, names `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` and states the no-edit and deep-loop gates | The T052 verify commands print what they say. Met 2026-11-13: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $ARM` prints nothing, and the `mutating\\?`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\\.policy` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` counts each print 1. | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:91:- [x] T009 Offer no hub command on a no-edit prompt (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: create `CAG` with three cases: `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-skill'), 'use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet')` returns `undefined`, the same call without `, do not change anything yet` returns `/create:skill` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test('just show me the plan')` is true. Then add `export const NO_EDIT_REQUEST` to `CA` with the pattern `fusion.ts` declares today and its comment, and in `attachCommand`, after the route shape checks, return `undefined` when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())`. Add a comment saying a reader who rules out a change gets no command from either path, so the hub route never offers what the scorer already withholds. Leave `FU` to T012. Verify: before the change `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports failures, after it 0 failed, `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:94:- [x] T012 Read the shared no-edit pattern in the scorer and drop the empty branch (`FU`). Add `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` to the existing import from `../command-attach.js`, delete the local `const NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and the comment above it, and delete the `if` on `semantic (code )?search` in `primaryIntentBonus`, whose body is empty. Verify: `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing, `rg -c \"semantic \\(code\" $FU` prints nothing, `TC` exits 0 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print their lines in `$SP/before.txt`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:96:- [x] T014 Name the guards and the policy table in the two READMEs (`CBR`, `LR`). In `CBR`, delete the sentence that says the block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES` and add that a surface attaching a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. In `LR`'s `command-attach.ts` row, replace the sentence about `/deep:` with `A system-deep-loop command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a DEPTH_WORDING phrase, and a prompt that matches NO_EDIT_REQUEST gets no command.` and keep `The module has no imports.` Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $CBR $LR` prints nothing, `rg -o \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\" $CBR | wc -l` prints at least 2, where it printed 1 before, and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $LR` prints 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:124:- [x] T032 Pin the four workflow promises in a contract test first (`DSCT`). Create `DSCT` reading `DSY`, `DSM`, `DSP` and `DSC` as `doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs` reads its files, with one test each: the delivery step says `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed` and no longer pairs that state with `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, and the `DSP` delivery row names the absent entry's printed repair. The `DSC` output block names the hook check's exit 1 as `STATUS=WARN` and its exit 2 as `STATUS=FAIL`. The `mutation_boundaries` invariant of `DSY` names `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`. The advisor step of `DSY` and `DSM` both name `hook health not recorded`, and `DSY` names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`. Verify: `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 4`, because no edit is in yet.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:154:- [x] T052 Give the row shape, the policy source and the gates as the code applies them (`ARM`). In the contract paragraph, give the row shape as `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, say `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads and replace the `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` sentence with one saying the attached command takes its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command. In the attach paragraph, replace the `system-deep-loop` sentence with one saying the prompt must type the same command or hold a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and add that a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"mutating\\?\" $ARM` prints 1, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\\.policy\" $ARM` prints 1 and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $ARM` prints 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:183:- [x] T058 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the six probes in `PL` after the build and append their output. Verify: the file holds `main returned 3`, `restored line: true`, `after: CLAUDE.md`, `plan exit=2`, a `ci.yml` line with equal digests, `undefined` on the no-edit, `/deep:ai-council` and both file-name lines of `probe-attach.mts`, `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in module -> false`, `(needs a mode)` on the first `probe-render.mjs` line and `(parent-named only)` on its second, and `probe-postwrite-foreign.cjs` prints 15 `apply exit 0` lines.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:264:- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -n \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $ADV/lib` lists `CA` and `FU` only, with `scorer/text.ts` holding the recorded third copy, and `rg -n \"isSymlink\\(\" $EMB` lists the root, router, mirror and `CLAUDE.md` checks. Evidence: `rg -n \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST|do not \\(change\" $ADV/lib` lists code lines only in `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/fusion.ts` and `scorer/text.ts:148`, plus the two READMEs that describe them. `rg -n \"isSymlink\\(\" $EMB` lists the root check at line 655, the router and mirror loop at line 827 and the `CLAUDE.md` checks at lines 852 and 1084.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:58:- **`command-attach.ts`**: the import-free module both the hub attach path and the scorer read. It gains the shared no-edit pattern and loses `COMMAND_POLICIES` through its deriver.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:64:A prompt reaches the advisor, the scorer ranks skills and command rows, and for a compiled-routing hub `enrichCompiledRoutes()` asks `attachCommand()` for a command, which now returns none on a no-edit prompt, a file name or an untyped deep-loop mention. `renderAdvisorBrief` prints the head the hooks inject. On the install side, `/doctor:agents-md embed` composes in memory, backs up, writes and proves, and any failure after the backup now ends in a verified restore or a printed refusal to restore.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:77:| `command-attach.ts` `attachCommand`, `typedCommandIn`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` | Producer of the attached and typed command | update | T009 to T011 cases in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `probe-attach.mts` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:79:| `scorer/fusion.ts` `readOnlyRouteAllowed`, `commandMeaningEligible` | Second reader of the no-edit wording | update to import | `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing and the scorer suite passes |\n=== hook check docs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:50:A fault in the middle of an embed now ends in a verified restore or a printed reason why not, and it exits 3. The hub attach path no longer offers a writing command on a no-edit prompt, a file name or a mention of another deep-loop command. The renderer tests pass inside a dispatched child. A live behaviour arm now runs only in a marked arena with an allowlisted environment.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:56:`command-attach.ts` now owns `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, and `fusion.ts` imports it. The deep-loop gate opens only for the command being attached or for depth wording. A dot or a slash followed by a word character continues a file name, so `/create:skill.md` is no typed command. The deriver no longer emits `COMMAND_POLICIES`, and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` is the one attach-path table.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:72:| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modified, Created | The shared no-edit pattern, the deep-loop gate, the file-name boundary and the absent policy table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:73:| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modified | Imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and drops an empty branch |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:112:| The shared `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` pattern stays as it is. This was decided without the operator, under goal decision D1, with no code change | A prompt that only limits the scope of a change, such as \"create a skill and do not change the existing skills\", keeps its skill and loses the command. That fails toward no offer and matches what the scorer path already did |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:135:| T058 probes | `main returned 3`, `restored line: true`, `after: CLAUDE.md`, `plan exit=2` with `ci.yml` digests `b8ae3686e91b` before and after, `undefined` on the no-edit, `/deep:ai-council` and file-name lines, `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in module -> false`, `(needs a mode)` and `(parent-named only)` on the two render lines and 15 `apply exit 0` lines |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:161:4. **A third copy of the no-edit wording remains.** `scorer/text.ts` line 148 keeps its own pattern. The plan records it, and this phase may not edit that file.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the prompt `use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet`, When the hub attach runs on its single `sk-create-skill` route, Then no command is attached, and `FU` reads the same `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` | `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` and `rg -c \"semantic \\(code\" $FU` print nothing. Met 2026-11-13: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports `14 passed (14)`, and both `rg -c` commands on `FU` print nothing and exit 1. `probe-attach.mts` prints `-> undefined` for the no-edit prompt. | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:88:| AC-033 | REQ-033 | Given `advisor-recommend.md`, When it is read, Then it gives the row shape with `mutating?`, names `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` and states the no-edit and deep-loop gates | The T052 verify commands print what they say. Met 2026-11-13: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $ARM` prints nothing, and the `mutating\\?`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\\.policy` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` counts each print 1. | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:91:- [x] T009 Offer no hub command on a no-edit prompt (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: create `CAG` with three cases: `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-skill'), 'use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet')` returns `undefined`, the same call without `, do not change anything yet` returns `/create:skill` and `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test('just show me the plan')` is true. Then add `export const NO_EDIT_REQUEST` to `CA` with the pattern `fusion.ts` declares today and its comment, and in `attachCommand`, after the route shape checks, return `undefined` when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())`. Add a comment saying a reader who rules out a change gets no command from either path, so the hub route never offers what the scorer already withholds. Leave `FU` to T012. Verify: before the change `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports failures, after it 0 failed, `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:94:- [x] T012 Read the shared no-edit pattern in the scorer and drop the empty branch (`FU`). Add `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` to the existing import from `../command-attach.js`, delete the local `const NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and the comment above it, and delete the `if` on `semantic (code )?search` in `primaryIntentBonus`, whose body is empty. Verify: `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing, `rg -c \"semantic \\(code\" $FU` prints nothing, `TC` exits 0 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print their lines in `$SP/before.txt`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:96:- [x] T014 Name the guards and the policy table in the two READMEs (`CBR`, `LR`). In `CBR`, delete the sentence that says the block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES` and add that a surface attaching a command reads its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. In `LR`'s `command-attach.ts` row, replace the sentence about `/deep:` with `A system-deep-loop command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a DEPTH_WORDING phrase, and a prompt that matches NO_EDIT_REQUEST gets no command.` and keep `The module has no imports.` Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $CBR $LR` prints nothing, `rg -o \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\" $CBR | wc -l` prints at least 2, where it printed 1 before, and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $LR` prints 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:124:- [x] T032 Pin the four workflow promises in a contract test first (`DSCT`). Create `DSCT` reading `DSY`, `DSM`, `DSP` and `DSC` as `doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs` reads its files, with one test each: the delivery step says `WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed` and no longer pairs that state with `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, and the `DSP` delivery row names the absent entry's printed repair. The `DSC` output block names the hook check's exit 1 as `STATUS=WARN` and its exit 2 as `STATUS=FAIL`. The `mutation_boundaries` invariant of `DSY` names `/tmp/system-skill-advisor`. The advisor step of `DSY` and `DSM` both name `hook health not recorded`, and `DSY` names `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG`. Verify: `NT $DSCT` reports `fail 4`, because no edit is in yet.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:154:- [x] T052 Give the row shape, the policy source and the gates as the code applies them (`ARM`). In the contract paragraph, give the row shape as `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }`, say `mutating` is the class the renderer's child downgrade reads and replace the `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` sentence with one saying the attached command takes its policy from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command. In the attach paragraph, replace the `system-deep-loop` sentence with one saying the prompt must type the same command or hold a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and add that a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $ARM` prints nothing, `rg -c \"mutating\\?\" $ARM` prints 1, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\\.policy\" $ARM` prints 1 and `rg -c \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $ARM` prints 1.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:183:- [x] T058 [C] Rerun the reproductions (`$SP/repro-after.txt`). Run the six probes in `PL` after the build and append their output. Verify: the file holds `main returned 3`, `restored line: true`, `after: CLAUDE.md`, `plan exit=2`, a `ci.yml` line with equal digests, `undefined` on the no-edit, `/deep:ai-council` and both file-name lines of `probe-attach.mts`, `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in module -> false`, `(needs a mode)` on the first `probe-render.mjs` line and `(parent-named only)` on its second, and `probe-postwrite-foreign.cjs` prints 15 `apply exit 0` lines.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/tasks.md:264:- [x] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -n \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $ADV/lib` lists `CA` and `FU` only, with `scorer/text.ts` holding the recorded third copy, and `rg -n \"isSymlink\\(\" $EMB` lists the root, router, mirror and `CLAUDE.md` checks. Evidence: `rg -n \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST|do not \\(change\" $ADV/lib` lists code lines only in `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/fusion.ts` and `scorer/text.ts:148`, plus the two READMEs that describe them. `rg -n \"isSymlink\\(\" $EMB` lists the root check at line 655, the router and mirror loop at line 827 and the `CLAUDE.md` checks at lines 852 and 1084.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:58:- **`command-attach.ts`**: the import-free module both the hub attach path and the scorer read. It gains the shared no-edit pattern and loses `COMMAND_POLICIES` through its deriver.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:64:A prompt reaches the advisor, the scorer ranks skills and command rows, and for a compiled-routing hub `enrichCompiledRoutes()` asks `attachCommand()` for a command, which now returns none on a no-edit prompt, a file name or an untyped deep-loop mention. `renderAdvisorBrief` prints the head the hooks inject. On the install side, `/doctor:agents-md embed` composes in memory, backs up, writes and proves, and any failure after the backup now ends in a verified restore or a printed refusal to restore.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:77:| `command-attach.ts` `attachCommand`, `typedCommandIn`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` | Producer of the attached and typed command | update | T009 to T011 cases in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `probe-attach.mts` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/plan.md:79:| `scorer/fusion.ts` `readOnlyRouteAllowed`, `commandMeaningEligible` | Second reader of the no-edit wording | update to import | `rg -c \"const NO_EDIT_REQUEST\" $FU` prints nothing and the scorer suite passes |\n=== hook check docs\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:40:  hook_wiring_check: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:61:    - \"Leg delivery: run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\" and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root \\\"$PWD\\\", and show each line they print under the leg. Both exit 0 is PASS. A hook-missing line is DEGRADED, with repair /doctor:runtime-mirrors in a Skilled checkout or /doctor:symlink check in a linked project. WARN codex-hooks-unapproved is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. WARN codex-advisor-hook-absent is DEGRADED, with the repair line the check printed. Exit 2 from either check is ERROR. This leg is never FAIL, because a hook that is not wired or not approved stops the brief, not the install.\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:37:  hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60:    - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && S=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build && grep -rn \\\"NO_EDIT\\\\|no-edit\\\\|no edit\\\\|make no changes\\\\|just show\\\" $S --include=*.md | grep -v review/ | head -20; echo \\\"=== hook check docs\\\"; grep -rn \\\"hook-wiring-check\\\" .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.md --include=*.yaml | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597930107,"end":1794597931395}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794597932513,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"id":"prt_1d65f4de1001YFYDUeB0Agrg9j","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65f0c2f001gT08TMqAGLSMuo","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":694,"output":161,"reasoning":969,"cache":{"read":188672,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794597937413,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"id":"prt_1d65f6105001JFRtYUzCVIprxF","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65f4de60013S0mTzYMG2mGao","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794597952468,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d65f953d002hlc4X5sgTbI17l","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d65f4de60013S0mTzYMG2mGao","type":"tool","id":"call_7beb7d2fd2514007bbef33ff","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\\|no-edit\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | head -20; echo \"=== lookahead\"; grep -rn \"lookahead\\|make no changes to\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.md --include=*.ts --include=*.cjs | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:126:**Scorer.** Five lanes fuse into a single calibrated score: explicit author signals, lexical overlap, skill-graph causality, derived metadata, and a semantic shadow lane. The fusion respects per-lane weights and emits per-lane attribution alongside the final score. Command detail lives in `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and lane semantics live in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md`. Command rows get vectors of their own in a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table that the skill-graph scan fills from each row's generated `embeddingText`. The semantic lane's real cosine against those vectors is the second way a command row can pass, beside its own phrases. The pass needs a cosine of at least 0.72 and a 0.02 lead over the next command row. A no-edit prompt rules out every command on meaning, and a read-only question admits only a read-only command. With no live embedder the rule never fires.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:219:The corpus now has 176 rows. One held-out prompt moved to the tuning set, and a new one took its place. That is why the tuning set counts 45. Without the embedder, rows match whole phrases. So they miss the held-out paraphrases. With the real embedder the held-out set reaches 2 of 44. That misses the target of 5. The held-out set was measured three times. The first round used a bar of 0.74 and no margin. It reached 4. The second round led each text with the job sentence and used the current bars. It reached 3. The third run followed the no-edit fix and reached 2. That fix took away one held-out hit. Its prompt is classed as a read-only question and had been answered by `/speckit:resume`, a command that is not read-only. The bars came from the tuning set only. Typed prompts stay at 24 of 44.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:157:| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 17 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:55:| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:132:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\n=== lookahead\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/v4/core/regexes.cjs:76:// Single character class, not an alternation: the two properties overlap (U+1F9B0-U+1F9B3), so `(A|B)+` backtracks exponentially on a failed match. The leading lookahead then demands one anchor — a pictograph, a regional indicator, or the enclosing keycap — because `\\p{Emoji_Component}` on its own covers ASCII digits, `#`, `*`, ZWJ, variation selectors and skin tone modifiers, none of which is an emoji without a base.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/src/v4/core/regexes.ts:63:// Single character class, not an alternation: the two properties overlap (U+1F9B0-U+1F9B3), so `(A|B)+` backtracks exponentially on a failed match. The leading lookahead then demands one anchor — a pictograph, a regional indicator, or the enclosing keycap — because `\\p{Emoji_Component}` on its own covers ASCII digits, `#`, `*`, ZWJ, variation selectors and skin tone modifiers, none of which is an emoji without a base.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/src/v4/core/tests/email-regex.test.ts:5:// the lookahead form `regexes.email` had before this rewrite\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:81:    'show me the plan and make no changes to the files',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:82:    'refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289:// Words alone cannot tell \"make no changes to the files\" from a change request\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:126:**Scorer.** Five lanes fuse into a single calibrated score: explicit author signals, lexical overlap, skill-graph causality, derived metadata, and a semantic shadow lane. The fusion respects per-lane weights and emits per-lane attribution alongside the final score. Command detail lives in `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and lane semantics live in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md`. Command rows get vectors of their own in a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table that the skill-graph scan fills from each row's generated `embeddingText`. The semantic lane's real cosine against those vectors is the second way a command row can pass, beside its own phrases. The pass needs a cosine of at least 0.72 and a 0.02 lead over the next command row. A no-edit prompt rules out every command on meaning, and a read-only question admits only a read-only command. With no live embedder the rule never fires.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/changelog/v1.0.0.0.md:219:The corpus now has 176 rows. One held-out prompt moved to the tuning set, and a new one took its place. That is why the tuning set counts 45. Without the embedder, rows match whole phrases. So they miss the held-out paraphrases. With the real embedder the held-out set reaches 2 of 44. That misses the target of 5. The held-out set was measured three times. The first round used a bar of 0.74 and no margin. It reached 4. The second round led each text with the job sentence and used the current bars. It reached 3. The third run followed the no-edit fix and reached 2. That fix took away one held-out hit. Its prompt is classed as a read-only question and had been answered by `/speckit:resume`, a command that is not read-only. The bars came from the tuning set only. Typed prompts stay at 24 of 44.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/README.md:157:| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 17 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/README.md:55:| `fusion.ts` | Combines lane scores into final advisor ranking signals through RRF fusion, with a conflict-match rerank seam and a self-recommendation guard that penalizes advisor self-recommendations. `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` keeps a passing command row passing only when the explicit-author lane matched one of its own phrases or its slash string, or when it passes on meaning: a real embedder cosine of at least `COMMAND_MEANING_MIN_COSINE` (0.72) with a lead of `COMMAND_MEANING_MARGIN` (0.02) over the next command row. The word-overlap stand-in used under test never counts. `commandMeaningEligible` decides who may pass on meaning: a prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, the pattern `readOnlyRouteAllowed` also reads, rules out every command, and a read-only explainer admits only a command whose route only reads. `rankMeaningPassedCommandFirst` moves a meaning-passed command ahead of the top passing skill only when its cosine leads that skill's by the same margin. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:132:| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. The module has no imports. |\n=== lookahead\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/v4/core/regexes.cjs:76:// Single character class, not an alternation: the two properties overlap (U+1F9B0-U+1F9B3), so `(A|B)+` backtracks exponentially on a failed match. The leading lookahead then demands one anchor — a pictograph, a regional indicator, or the enclosing keycap — because `\\p{Emoji_Component}` on its own covers ASCII digits, `#`, `*`, ZWJ, variation selectors and skin tone modifiers, none of which is an emoji without a base.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/src/v4/core/regexes.ts:63:// Single character class, not an alternation: the two properties overlap (U+1F9B0-U+1F9B3), so `(A|B)+` backtracks exponentially on a failed match. The leading lookahead then demands one anchor — a pictograph, a regional indicator, or the enclosing keycap — because `\\p{Emoji_Component}` on its own covers ASCII digits, `#`, `*`, ZWJ, variation selectors and skin tone modifiers, none of which is an emoji without a base.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/node_modules/zod/src/v4/core/tests/email-regex.test.ts:5:// the lookahead form `regexes.email` had before this rewrite\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:81:    'show me the plan and make no changes to the files',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:82:    'refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api',\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:289:// Words alone cannot tell \"make no changes to the files\" from a change request\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"NO_EDIT_REQUEST\\\\|no-edit\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor --include=*.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== lookahead\\\"; grep -rn \\\"lookahead\\\\|make no changes to\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor .skilled/commands/doctor --include=*.md --include=*.ts --include=*.cjs | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794597950781,"end":1794597952468}}}}
