{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794598009367,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d66077be001MOCophuGk1191s","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d6603514001MxgQ2deN4Ljaq7","type":"tool","id":"call_78e49c879b5d419c905e27eb","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '150,170p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md"},"output":"| `plan.md` section 4 names nine wave 4 lanes, T062 to T072 | `tasks.md` runs ten lanes, T062 to T073 | T073 was added to the task list after the plan was written, and `plan.md` was not updated |\n| T070's verify pattern is `headerOf\\(filePath\\)` | The pattern ends in the call's semicolon | The first pattern also matched the helper's own signature |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:limitations -->\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **The hook-wiring matcher misreads some shell shapes.** It reads `true; node <script>` and `cd x;node <script>` as missing and `echo 'x && node <script>'` as wired. It also reads `node --no-warnings <script>`, `/usr/bin/env node <script>` and `zsh -c 'node <script>'` as missing. No Skilled installer writes any of these shapes, so this is recorded and not built.\n2. **The new Pi reader test compares against an unresolved temp path.** A regression that opened the resolved path would still pass it.\n3. **Two holdout guards change nothing today.** The `typedRows` and `attachedRows` guards in the capture script filter nothing on today's corpus, because only `rows` ever held holdout ids.\n4. **A third copy of the no-edit wording remains.** `scorer/text.ts` line 148 keeps its own pattern. The plan records it, and this phase may not edit that file.\n5. **Review pass two has not run.** It reviews this code and is the packet's gate, not this phase's.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"| `plan.md` section 4 names nine wave 4 lanes, T062 to T072 | `tasks.md` runs ten lanes, T062 to T073 | T073 was added to the task list after the plan was written, and `plan.md` was not updated |\n| T070's verify pattern is `headerOf\\(filePath\\)` | The pattern ends in the call's semicolon | The first pattern also matched the helper's own signature |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:limitations -->\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **The hook-wiring matcher misreads some shell shapes.** It reads `true; node <script>` and `cd x;node <script>` as missing and `echo 'x && node <script>'` as wired. It also reads `node --no-warnings <script>`, `/usr/bin/env node <script>` and `zsh -c 'node <script>'` as missing. No Skilled installer writes any of these shapes, so this is recorded and not built.\n2. **The new Pi reader test compares against an unresolved temp path.** A regression that opened the resolved path would still pass it.\n3. **Two holdout guards change nothing today.** The `typedRows` and `attachedRows` guards in the capture script filter nothing on today's corpus, because only `rows` ever held holdout ids.\n4. **A third copy of the no-edit wording remains.** `scorer/text.ts` line 148 keeps its own pattern. The plan records it, and this phase may not edit that file.\n5. **Review pass two has not run.** It reviews this code and is the packet's gate, not this phase's.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:limitations -->\n\n---\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '150,170p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794598008766,"end":1794598009367}}}}
