{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794598199063,"sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","part":{"partID":"prt_1d662c758001yJtoGPVD27g18Y","sessionID":"ses_e29b1d959ffeIRu3GDOv5mxZKO","messageID":"msg_1d662ae13001HeDWPZ9T7Kc4tr","type":"tool","id":"call_244cf265a7f74fd9b10c5359","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report - Command Surfacing, Pass Three Closing Round (noedit-close-3c lineage)\n\n- Run: `fanout-noedit-close-3c-1794596804847-827gze`\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Base / HEAD: `846eab66b8984c0e745a768fcc12f176ebdf1991` (the final pass-three commit)\n- Lineage artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c`\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (3 of 3; the third iteration added no new finding)\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\n- hasAdvisories: **false** (the algorithm reserves `true` for a PASS carrying P2; this run has an active P1, and two active P2 are listed below as advisories)\n- Active findings: **P0 0, P1 1, P2 2**\n- Review scope: the final state of the no-edit gate (`NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, `isNoEditRequest`) and its three callers, then the doctor hook check (`readWords`, `simpleCommands`, `commandWords`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript`, `runsNodeOnMarker`, `scriptWord`, `runsMarker`), each with its test file.\n- Operator review focus: \"Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE closing round. FIRST read the full instructions in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3c.txt and follow them exactly, including the two settled decisions you must not report again. Scope: the final state of the doctor hook check and the no-edit pattern. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input you ran. Finding nothing new is a valid result. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder.\"\n\n### What this lineage did with the two settled decisions\n\n| Settled decision | Handling |\n|---|---|\n| \"make no changes\" rules out a change whatever follows it | Not re-reported. The settled control was run once (`refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api` → matched, no command) and left alone. |\n| The hook check is a wiring heuristic, not a node or shell parser | Not re-reported. `bash -o pipefail -c` and `command node` misreads are recorded as edge cases in iteration 2, not findings. |\n\n### The two review areas, judged\n\n| Area | New findings | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| No-edit gate | **P1 1, P2 1** | `don't create it yet` / `don't write the file yet` are not matched and keep `/create:changelog`; `just show … then create it` is matched and loses it, while the same sentence without \"just\" keeps it. Both were run through the shipped modules. |\n| Doctor hook check | **P2 1** | A valid `node --env-file .env <marker>` reports `hook-missing` exit 1, while `node --env-file=.env <marker>` reports `ok` exit 0. Run as a process against a `mktemp` checkout. |\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is required for this lineage: the verdict is CONDITIONAL because `NC3-P1-001` is active. The P1 is a one-line widening of the negative-instruction verb list plus tests; the two P2 advisories can ride along.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NC3-P1-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"title\": \"NO_EDIT_REQUEST omits the write verbs, so \\\"don't create it yet\\\" keeps a mutating command\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"class-of-bug\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"the matcher is the changed line and the attach gate is its caller (:338); the probe prompt is a hub naming prompt with one selected mode, the shape attachCommand requires\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"hub command attachment\", \"/create:* mutating offers\", \"shared matcher consumed by fusion.ts:677, fusion.ts:881 and text.ts:150\"],\n      \"evidence\": \"use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet -> isNoEditRequest false, isReadOnlyExplainer false, attachCommand returns /create:changelog; control with don't change anything yet -> undefined\",\n      \"disposition\": \"required\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NC3-P2-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"\\\"just show\\\" and \\\"just list\\\" read a two-step change request as a no-edit request\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"class-of-bug\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"both prompts exercise the changed matcher through the hub gate at :338 with the same single-mode route; the only input difference is the word just\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"hub command attachment\", \"two-step look-first-then-change prompts\", \"shared matcher read-only branches\"],\n      \"evidence\": \"just show me the changelog draft, then create it -> matcher true, command undefined; show me the changelog draft, then create it -> matcher false, command /create:changelog\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NC3-P2-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"title\": \"A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script, so a wired hook reports hook-missing\",\n      \"dimension\": \"correctness\",\n      \"file\": \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222\",\n      \"findingClass\": \"class-of-bug\",\n      \"scopeProof\": \"the skip is on the reviewed line (the NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT set at :222, consumed at :277) and the probe command is a valid node invocation that runs the hook script named in the settings file\",\n      \"affectedSurfaceHints\": [\"/doctor hook wiring diagnosis\", \"claude/codex/cursor/devin hook rows\", \"doctor-setup and doctor-symlink-check delivery legs\"],\n      \"evidence\": \"settings command node --env-file .env <marker> -> hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json exit 1; node --env-file=.env <marker> -> ok claude exit 0\",\n      \"disposition\": \"advisory\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": [\n    {\n      \"order\": 1,\n      \"severity\": \"P1\",\n      \"findings\": [\"NC3-P1-001\"],\n      \"action\": \"Extend the negative-instruction alternative to the write verbs a reader actually uses (create, write, save, and their relatives) and add a genuine no-edit case with an object to command-attach-guards.vitest.ts that calls attachCommand, not only the matcher.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"order\": 2,\n      \"severity\": \"P2\",\n      \"findings\": [\"NC3-P2-002\", \"NC3-P2-003\"],\n      \"action\": \"Anchor the just show / just list markers to the end of the request, or require that no write verb follows in the same sentence; add --env-file and --title to the node argument-taking flag set with the separated and attached forms as two test rows.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Record the rule the matcher must honour: a negative instruction rules out the change whichever write verb names it, and a read-only opener that is followed by a change verb is not a no-edit request.\",\n    \"Record that the hook check reads a node launch word by word, including a flag whose value stands in the next word.\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add the failing probe as a case: use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet (no-edit, no command).\",\n    \"Add the paired control: use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't change anything yet (already matched).\",\n    \"Add the two-step case: just show me the changelog draft, then create it keeps /create:changelog.\",\n    \"Add a hook case for node --env-file .env <marker> expecting ok, beside the existing node --no-warnings row.\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"class-of-bug\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\",\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\",\n    \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | File:line | Evidence | Impact | Fix recommendation | Disposition | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|-----------|----------|--------|--------------------|-------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\n| NC3-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | NO_EDIT_REQUEST omits the write verbs, so \"don't create it yet\" keeps a mutating command | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292` | `isNoEditRequest('use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet')` false; `attachCommand` returns `/create:changelog`; the control with `don't change anything yet` returns `undefined` | A reader who rules out the creation is handed a `mutates` command offer, the exact failure the guard exists to prevent | Add create/write/save to the negative-instruction alternative and pin an object-bearing no-edit case through `attachCommand` | required | class-of-bug | matcher on the changed line; gate at `:338`; route mode `sk-create-changelog` is `mutatesWorkspace: true` in `mode-registry.json:317-336` | hub attach path; `/create:*`; three shared-matcher callers |\n| NC3-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | \"just show\" and \"just list\" read a two-step change request as a no-edit request | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292` | `just show me the changelog draft, then create it` → matcher true, no command; without \"just\" → matcher false, `/create:changelog` | A change request loses its command offer because of one read-only opener | Anchor the marker to the end of the request or require no write verb after it | advisory | class-of-bug | same matcher, same gate, one-word input difference | hub attach path; two-step prompts |\n| NC3-P2-003 | P2 | correctness | A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` | `node --env-file .env <marker>` → `hook-missing` exit 1; `node --env-file=.env <marker>` → `ok` exit 0; node accepts both forms | A correctly wired hook is reported missing and the operator chases the wrong repair | Add the argument-taking flags outside the module-loader family (`--env-file`, `--title`) to the set | advisory | class-of-bug | skip at `:277`; valid node invocation; no shell construct | `/doctor` hook wiring diagnosis; four runtime rows; two doctor delivery legs |\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n### P0\n\nNone.\n\n### P1\n\n1. **Widen the negative-instruction verbs (`NC3-P1-001`).** In `command-attach.ts:292`, extend `(?:do not|don't) (change|edit|modify|touch)` to the write verbs a reader uses when refusing work (`create`, `write`, `save`). Add to `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` a case that calls `attachCommand` with a single-mode `sk-create-changelog` route on `use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet` and expects `undefined`, plus the `don't write` and `don't save` variants at the matcher level.\n\n### P2 advisories (separate, non-blocking)\n\n2. **Anchor the read-only markers (`NC3-P2-002`).** Make `just show` / `just list` match only when the request does not continue into a change, or move them to a list of openers that a later write verb overrides. Add the paired rows (`just show … then create it` → no match; `show … then create it` → match stays as today).\n3. **Complete the node argument set (`NC3-P2-003`).** Add `--env-file` and `--title` to `NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT`, with one test row for the separated form next to the existing `node --no-warnings` row. Leave the quoted-value and shell-grammar cases to the settled decision.\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- The no-edit contract should say that a negative instruction rules out the change whichever write verb names it, and that an object after the phrase never decides the reading alone (the settled cost stays).\n- The no-edit contract should say that a read-only opener followed by a change verb is a change request, not a refusal.\n- The hook contract should say that the check reads a node launch word by word, including a flag whose value stands in the next word, and that shell-grammar shapes remain out of scope by decision.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- Add the failing no-edit probe as an `attachCommand` test: `use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet` → `undefined`.\n- Add the matcher rows for `don't write the file yet` and `do not save them yet`.\n- Add the two-step rows: `just show me the changelog draft, then create it` keeps `/create:changelog`; `show me the changelog draft, then create it` stays as today.\n- Add the hook row: settings command `node --env-file .env <marker>` → `ok claude` exit 0.\n- Run the two single test files named in the review focus, not the full suite.\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Drift |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | pass with the two findings standing as the gap | `runtime/lib/README.md:132`, `scorer/README.md:55`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33` all describe the final code | none |\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60` (AC-005) claims the no-edit prompt attaches nothing and `fusion.ts` reads the same pattern; both hold | the two pass-three commits are post-acceptance remediation with no checklist row of their own |\n\nAC_COVERAGE: **disabled** — the advisory signal applies only when the validation rule runs for a Level 2+ spec folder; this lineage did not run validation and makes no claim from it.\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Drift |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:36` names the same four markers and both gates | none |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | partial | `doctor-setup.yaml:61` and `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` describe the check's exit roles correctly; all four runtime files in this checkout print `ok` | `NC3-P2-003` is one valid launch inside the model that still reports exit 1 |\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | no agent or command document changed in scope | none |\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook surface in either file | none |\n\nSecurity was assessed in iteration 3 as a no-applicable-surface audit: neither module executes reviewed input, the matcher pattern is a literal with no user-built pattern, and the hook check only reads JSON and compares strings.\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- The stale `014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md` \"Known Limitations\" rows (items 1 and 4) describe the pre-pass-two state. The section dates itself with \"Review pass two has not run\", so it is historical context, not a live claim; updating it belongs to the phase-014 owner, not this review.\n- The shell-grammar shapes the hook check does not read (`bash -o pipefail -c`, `command node`) stay deferred under the second settled decision.\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0\n- Swept directions: none\n- Selected review directions: no-edit gate correctness (iteration 1), hook check correctness (iteration 2), traceability and maintainability (iteration 3)\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the loop hit the iteration cap with the frontier empty\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence summary\n\n| Iteration | Dimension | New findings | newFindingsRatio | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | correctness (no-edit gate) | P1 1, P2 1 | 1.0 | complete |\n| 2 | correctness (hook check) | P2 1 | 1.0 | complete |\n| 3 | traceability + maintainability | none | 0 | complete |\n\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (iteration cap 3; the third iteration added no finding, so no fourth pass was available to confirm stabilization)\n- Convergence score at close: 1.00 (reducer); release-readiness state: `in-progress`\n- Verdict derivation: active P0 = 0, active P1 = 1 → CONDITIONAL\n\n### Coverage summary\n\n| Dimension | Covered | Iterations | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| correctness | yes | 1, 2 | no-edit gate and hook check |\n| traceability | yes | 3 | core and overlay status above |\n| maintainability | yes | 3 | comments, docs, test comments |\n| security | assessed | 3 | no-applicable-surface audit; no iteration record emitted |\n\n### Ruled-out claims\n\n- Regex backtracking, `lastIndex` state, non-string input, and the curly-apostrophe fold (iteration 1).\n- Crash/hang in the hook check, marker-suffix false positives, vacuous launch tests (iteration 2).\n- Stale third pattern copy, stale lookahead prose, crossed doctor exit codes, an unstated runtime row (iteration 3).\n\n### Sources reviewed\n\n- The two changed source files, their two test files, the three shared-matcher callers, the packet's AC-005 row, the phase-014 known-limitations list, the two feature-catalog rows, the two library README rows, the sk-doc mode-registry entry, and the two doctor delivery assets.\n- Never opened: `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or any holdout prompt text.\n\n### Cross-reference appendix\n\n- `Core Protocols`: `spec_code` pass-with-gaps, `checklist_evidence` partial.\n- `Overlay Protocols`: `feature_catalog_code` pass, `agent_cross_runtime` partial, `skill_agent` notApplicable, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report - Command Surfacing, Pass Three Closing Round (noedit-close-3c lineage)\\n\\n- Run: `fanout-noedit-close-3c-1794596804847-827gze`\\n- Target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Base / HEAD: `846eab66b8984c0e745a768fcc12f176ebdf1991` (the final pass-three commit)\\n- Lineage artifact directory: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c`\\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (3 of 3; the third iteration added no new finding)\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- Overall verdict: **CONDITIONAL**\\n- hasAdvisories: **false** (the algorithm reserves `true` for a PASS carrying P2; this run has an active P1, and two active P2 are listed below as advisories)\\n- Active findings: **P0 0, P1 1, P2 2**\\n- Review scope: the final state of the no-edit gate (`NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, `isNoEditRequest`) and its three callers, then the doctor hook check (`readWords`, `simpleCommands`, `commandWords`, `nodeFlagSkipsScript`, `runsNodeOnMarker`, `scriptWord`, `runsMarker`), each with its test file.\\n- Operator review focus: \\\"Code review of command surfacing, PASS THREE closing round. FIRST read the full instructions in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/c9fe91ef-9b85-4bdc-88fb-4d6f766eaecf/scratchpad/review-instructions-3c.txt and follow them exactly, including the two settled decisions you must not report again. Scope: the final state of the doctor hook check and the no-edit pattern. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input you ran. Finding nothing new is a valid result. Never open holdout-prompts.jsonl. Change no code, write only inside your lineage folder.\\\"\\n\\n### What this lineage did with the two settled decisions\\n\\n| Settled decision | Handling |\\n|---|---|\\n| \\\"make no changes\\\" rules out a change whatever follows it | Not re-reported. The settled control was run once (`refactor the parser and make no changes to its public api` → matched, no command) and left alone. |\\n| The hook check is a wiring heuristic, not a node or shell parser | Not re-reported. `bash -o pipefail -c` and `command node` misreads are recorded as edge cases in iteration 2, not findings. |\\n\\n### The two review areas, judged\\n\\n| Area | New findings | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No-edit gate | **P1 1, P2 1** | `don't create it yet` / `don't write the file yet` are not matched and keep `/create:changelog`; `just show … then create it` is matched and loses it, while the same sentence without \\\"just\\\" keeps it. Both were run through the shipped modules. |\\n| Doctor hook check | **P2 1** | A valid `node --env-file .env <marker>` reports `hook-missing` exit 1, while `node --env-file=.env <marker>` reports `ok` exit 0. Run as a process against a `mktemp` checkout. |\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is required for this lineage: the verdict is CONDITIONAL because `NC3-P1-001` is active. The P1 is a one-line widening of the negative-instruction verb list plus tests; the two P2 advisories can ride along.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"NC3-P1-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"NO_EDIT_REQUEST omits the write verbs, so \\\\\\\"don't create it yet\\\\\\\" keeps a mutating command\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"the matcher is the changed line and the attach gate is its caller (:338); the probe prompt is a hub naming prompt with one selected mode, the shape attachCommand requires\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\\"hub command attachment\\\", \\\"/create:* mutating offers\\\", \\\"shared matcher consumed by fusion.ts:677, fusion.ts:881 and text.ts:150\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet -> isNoEditRequest false, isReadOnlyExplainer false, attachCommand returns /create:changelog; control with don't change anything yet -> undefined\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"required\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"NC3-P2-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"just show\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"just list\\\\\\\" read a two-step change request as a no-edit request\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"both prompts exercise the changed matcher through the hub gate at :338 with the same single-mode route; the only input difference is the word just\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\\"hub command attachment\\\", \\\"two-step look-first-then-change prompts\\\", \\\"shared matcher read-only branches\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"just show me the changelog draft, then create it -> matcher true, command undefined; show me the changelog draft, then create it -> matcher false, command /create:changelog\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"NC3-P2-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script, so a wired hook reports hook-missing\\\",\\n      \\\"dimension\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222\\\",\\n      \\\"findingClass\\\": \\\"class-of-bug\\\",\\n      \\\"scopeProof\\\": \\\"the skip is on the reviewed line (the NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT set at :222, consumed at :277) and the probe command is a valid node invocation that runs the hook script named in the settings file\\\",\\n      \\\"affectedSurfaceHints\\\": [\\\"/doctor hook wiring diagnosis\\\", \\\"claude/codex/cursor/devin hook rows\\\", \\\"doctor-setup and doctor-symlink-check delivery legs\\\"],\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"settings command node --env-file .env <marker> -> hook-missing claude .claude/settings.json exit 1; node --env-file=.env <marker> -> ok claude exit 0\\\",\\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"advisory\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\",\\n      \\\"findings\\\": [\\\"NC3-P1-001\\\"],\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Extend the negative-instruction alternative to the write verbs a reader actually uses (create, write, save, and their relatives) and add a genuine no-edit case with an object to command-attach-guards.vitest.ts that calls attachCommand, not only the matcher.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"order\\\": 2,\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\",\\n      \\\"findings\\\": [\\\"NC3-P2-002\\\", \\\"NC3-P2-003\\\"],\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Anchor the just show / just list markers to the end of the request, or require that no write verb follows in the same sentence; add --env-file and --title to the node argument-taking flag set with the separated and attached forms as two test rows.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Record the rule the matcher must honour: a negative instruction rules out the change whichever write verb names it, and a read-only opener that is followed by a change verb is not a no-edit request.\\\",\\n    \\\"Record that the hook check reads a node launch word by word, including a flag whose value stands in the next word.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add the failing probe as a case: use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet (no-edit, no command).\\\",\\n    \\\"Add the paired control: use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't change anything yet (already matched).\\\",\\n    \\\"Add the two-step case: just show me the changelog draft, then create it keeps /create:changelog.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add a hook case for node --env-file .env <marker> expecting ok, beside the existing node --no-warnings row.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"class-of-bug\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | File:line | Evidence | Impact | Fix recommendation | Disposition | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surface hints |\\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|-----------|----------|--------|--------------------|-------------|---------------|-------------|------------------------|\\n| NC3-P1-001 | P1 | correctness | NO_EDIT_REQUEST omits the write verbs, so \\\"don't create it yet\\\" keeps a mutating command | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292` | `isNoEditRequest('use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet')` false; `attachCommand` returns `/create:changelog`; the control with `don't change anything yet` returns `undefined` | A reader who rules out the creation is handed a `mutates` command offer, the exact failure the guard exists to prevent | Add create/write/save to the negative-instruction alternative and pin an object-bearing no-edit case through `attachCommand` | required | class-of-bug | matcher on the changed line; gate at `:338`; route mode `sk-create-changelog` is `mutatesWorkspace: true` in `mode-registry.json:317-336` | hub attach path; `/create:*`; three shared-matcher callers |\\n| NC3-P2-002 | P2 | correctness | \\\"just show\\\" and \\\"just list\\\" read a two-step change request as a no-edit request | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:292` | `just show me the changelog draft, then create it` → matcher true, no command; without \\\"just\\\" → matcher false, `/create:changelog` | A change request loses its command offer because of one read-only opener | Anchor the marker to the end of the request or require no write verb after it | advisory | class-of-bug | same matcher, same gate, one-word input difference | hub attach path; two-step prompts |\\n| NC3-P2-003 | P2 | correctness | A valid node flag whose value stands in the next word is read as the hook script | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:222` | `node --env-file .env <marker>` → `hook-missing` exit 1; `node --env-file=.env <marker>` → `ok` exit 0; node accepts both forms | A correctly wired hook is reported missing and the operator chases the wrong repair | Add the argument-taking flags outside the module-loader family (`--env-file`, `--title`) to the set | advisory | class-of-bug | skip at `:277`; valid node invocation; no shell construct | `/doctor` hook wiring diagnosis; four runtime rows; two doctor delivery legs |\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n### P0\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1\\n\\n1. **Widen the negative-instruction verbs (`NC3-P1-001`).** In `command-attach.ts:292`, extend `(?:do not|don't) (change|edit|modify|touch)` to the write verbs a reader uses when refusing work (`create`, `write`, `save`). Add to `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` a case that calls `attachCommand` with a single-mode `sk-create-changelog` route on `use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet` and expects `undefined`, plus the `don't write` and `don't save` variants at the matcher level.\\n\\n### P2 advisories (separate, non-blocking)\\n\\n2. **Anchor the read-only markers (`NC3-P2-002`).** Make `just show` / `just list` match only when the request does not continue into a change, or move them to a list of openers that a later write verb overrides. Add the paired rows (`just show … then create it` → no match; `show … then create it` → match stays as today).\\n3. **Complete the node argument set (`NC3-P2-003`).** Add `--env-file` and `--title` to `NODE_FLAGS_WITH_ARGUMENT`, with one test row for the separated form next to the existing `node --no-warnings` row. Leave the quoted-value and shell-grammar cases to the settled decision.\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- The no-edit contract should say that a negative instruction rules out the change whichever write verb names it, and that an object after the phrase never decides the reading alone (the settled cost stays).\\n- The no-edit contract should say that a read-only opener followed by a change verb is a change request, not a refusal.\\n- The hook contract should say that the check reads a node launch word by word, including a flag whose value stands in the next word, and that shell-grammar shapes remain out of scope by decision.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- Add the failing no-edit probe as an `attachCommand` test: `use sk-doc to plan the changelog, don't create it yet` → `undefined`.\\n- Add the matcher rows for `don't write the file yet` and `do not save them yet`.\\n- Add the two-step rows: `just show me the changelog draft, then create it` keeps `/create:changelog`; `show me the changelog draft, then create it` stays as today.\\n- Add the hook row: settings command `node --env-file .env <marker>` → `ok claude` exit 0.\\n- Run the two single test files named in the review focus, not the full suite.\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Drift |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | pass with the two findings standing as the gap | `runtime/lib/README.md:132`, `scorer/README.md:55`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33` all describe the final code | none |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | partial | `014-review-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60` (AC-005) claims the no-edit prompt attaches nothing and `fusion.ts` reads the same pattern; both hold | the two pass-three commits are post-acceptance remediation with no checklist row of their own |\\n\\nAC_COVERAGE: **disabled** — the advisory signal applies only when the validation rule runs for a Level 2+ spec folder; this lineage did not run validation and makes no claim from it.\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence | Drift |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | `command-meaning-matching.md:36` names the same four markers and both gates | none |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | partial | `doctor-setup.yaml:61` and `doctor-symlink-check.yaml:60` describe the check's exit roles correctly; all four runtime files in this checkout print `ok` | `NC3-P2-003` is one valid launch inside the model that still reports exit 1 |\\n| `skill_agent` | notApplicable | no agent or command document changed in scope | none |\\n| `playbook_capability` | notApplicable | no playbook surface in either file | none |\\n\\nSecurity was assessed in iteration 3 as a no-applicable-surface audit: neither module executes reviewed input, the matcher pattern is a literal with no user-built pattern, and the hook check only reads JSON and compares strings.\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- The stale `014-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md` \\\"Known Limitations\\\" rows (items 1 and 4) describe the pre-pass-two state. The section dates itself with \\\"Review pass two has not run\\\", so it is historical context, not a live claim; updating it belongs to the phase-014 owner, not this review.\\n- The shell-grammar shapes the hook check does not read (`bash -o pipefail -c`, `command node`) stay deferred under the second settled decision.\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0; failed pivots: 0; audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept directions: none\\n- Selected review directions: no-edit gate correctness (iteration 1), hook check correctness (iteration 2), traceability and maintainability (iteration 3)\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded; the loop hit the iteration cap with the frontier empty\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence summary\\n\\n| Iteration | Dimension | New findings | newFindingsRatio | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | correctness (no-edit gate) | P1 1, P2 1 | 1.0 | complete |\\n| 2 | correctness (hook check) | P2 1 | 1.0 | complete |\\n| 3 | traceability + maintainability | none | 0 | complete |\\n\\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (iteration cap 3; the third iteration added no finding, so no fourth pass was available to confirm stabilization)\\n- Convergence score at close: 1.00 (reducer); release-readiness state: `in-progress`\\n- Verdict derivation: active P0 = 0, active P1 = 1 → CONDITIONAL\\n\\n### Coverage summary\\n\\n| Dimension | Covered | Iterations | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| correctness | yes | 1, 2 | no-edit gate and hook check |\\n| traceability | yes | 3 | core and overlay status above |\\n| maintainability | yes | 3 | comments, docs, test comments |\\n| security | assessed | 3 | no-applicable-surface audit; no iteration record emitted |\\n\\n### Ruled-out claims\\n\\n- Regex backtracking, `lastIndex` state, non-string input, and the curly-apostrophe fold (iteration 1).\\n- Crash/hang in the hook check, marker-suffix false positives, vacuous launch tests (iteration 2).\\n- Stale third pattern copy, stale lookahead prose, crossed doctor exit codes, an unstated runtime row (iteration 3).\\n\\n### Sources reviewed\\n\\n- The two changed source files, their two test files, the three shared-matcher callers, the packet's AC-005 row, the phase-014 known-limitations list, the two feature-catalog rows, the two library README rows, the sk-doc mode-registry entry, and the two doctor delivery assets.\\n- Never opened: `holdout-prompts.jsonl` or any holdout prompt text.\\n\\n### Cross-reference appendix\\n\\n- `Core Protocols`: `spec_code` pass-with-gaps, `checklist_evidence` partial.\\n- `Overlay Protocols`: `feature_catalog_code` pass, `agent_cross_runtime` partial, `skill_agent` notApplicable, `playbook_capability` notApplicable.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/noedit-close-3c/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794598160216,"end":1794598199063}}}}
